<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Out-of-distribution (OOD).</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Out-of-distribution (OOD). ‣ 4.2 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mixture of Thoughts: Learning to Aggregate What Experts Think, Not Just What They Say" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows accuracy on <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PreAlgebra</span>, <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MBPP</span>, and <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">C-EVAL</span>. <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoT</span> achieves the best average (47.92), exceeding <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Avengers</span> (46.56) by <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{+2.92\%}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">2.92</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{+2.92\%}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">RouterDC</span> (45.85) by <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{+4.52\%}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">4.52</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{+4.52\%}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the strongest single-model baseline (Dolphin-2.9-LLaMA-3-8B; 43.95) by <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{+9.03\%}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">9.03</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{+9.03\%}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoT</span> is best on all three OOD tasks and maintains runtime on par with <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Avengers</span> (38.1 vs. 37.9 minutes). We attribute the stronger OOD generalization to latent-space collaboration via interaction layers: the primary expert can integrate hidden states from heterogeneous peers, going beyond single/multi-model routing or output-level aggregation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Out-of-distribution results (accuracy %).</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F5F7FA;">
