<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following previous work, we evaluate MoT using the Language Model Evaluation Harness <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.
Our default MoT configuration employs <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=8</annotation></semantics></math> stacks, top-<math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=3</annotation></semantics></math> routed experts, shared latent dimension <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{s}=2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{s}=2048</annotation></semantics></math>, router hidden size <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>768</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">768</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=8</annotation></semantics></math> attention heads in the interaction layers.
The router input encoder is DeBERTaV3-base <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, used as a frozen sentence encoder.
Training uses AdamW with learning rate <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math>, gradient clipping, weight decay <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> epochs with <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> warmup steps.
Regularization weights are set to <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{ent}}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>ent</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{ent}}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{bal}}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>bal</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{bal}}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{con}}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{con}}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>. For open-ended generation tasks we sample <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=10</annotation></semantics></math> outputs per query with temperature <math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math>. We train on NVIDIA A100 80 GB GPUs and perform inference on NVIDIA RTX A6000 48 GB GPUs.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Models</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate on seven open-source decoder-only LLMs in the 7B–8B range:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mistral family (5):</em> <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mistral-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> (general), <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MetaMath-Mistral-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> (MetaMathQA-tuned), <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Zephyr-7B-Beta</span> (DPO-aligned chat), <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Chinese-Mistral-7B</span> (vocabulary-expanded, continued pretraining on Chinese corpora), and <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">dolphin-2.6-mistral-7b</span> (instruction-tuned, Cognitive Computations).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Llama-3 family (2):</em> <span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama-3-8B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> (general) and <span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">dolphin-2.9-llama3-8b</span> (instruction-tuned, Cognitive Computations).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This pool mixes general, alignment-focused, domain-specialized, and multilingual experts while keeping scale comparable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Datasets</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">In-distribution.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MMLU</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> (57 subjects, broad knowledge);
(ii) <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GSM8K</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> (grade-school math);
(iii) <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CMMLU</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> (67 Chinese subjects);
(iv) <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ARC-Challenge (ARC-C)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> (multi-choice reasoning); and
(v) <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HumanEval</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> (Python code generation).
For GSM8K, we use its default train/test split; for the others, we randomly split 70%/30% following standard practice.
The union of all training sets forms the data to train the global router and interaction layers; evaluation is on the held-out test sets.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Out-of-distribution.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PreAlgebra</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> (algebraic problems);
(ii) <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MBPP</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> (1,000 Python coding tasks); and
(iii) <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C-Eval</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite> (52 Chinese subjects across four difficulty levels).
These datasets are unseen during training and used only for OOD evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Baselines</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We benchmark against a broad spectrum of routing/aggregation strategies:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CosineClassifier</em>: multi-class routing via a cosine-similarity classifier.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Voting</em>: query all experts and take the majority output.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZOOTER</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>: supervised router trained with reward-based scoring signals.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">LoraRetriever</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>: routing from query clustering as a proxy for task identity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">RouterDC</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>: supervised router using dual contrastive learning between queries and model embeddings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Avengers</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>: state-of-the-art training-free clustering with ensemble-style sampling and voting.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Together, these baselines span simple training-free heuristics and advanced supervised routers under a consistent evaluation protocol.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Training Strategy</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train only lightweight components—global router <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, per-expert/per-stack forward/reverse projectors, and shared cross-attention weights—while keeping all expert backbones frozen.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Primary objective.</span>
For input sequence <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and target sequence <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}=(y_{0},\ldots,y_{T-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}=(y_{0},\ldots,y_{T-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, the primary expert <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> predicts next-token distributions <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{m^{*}}(y_{t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{m^{*}}(y_{t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>. We minimize the autoregressive negative likelihood loss (NLL):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{LM}}\;=\;-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log p_{m^{*}}\!\left(y_{t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{&lt;t}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>LM</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{LM}}\;=\;-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log p_{m^{*}}\!\left(y_{t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{&lt;t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Router exploration (entropy).</span>
Let <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=\operatorname*{PromptEncoder}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">PromptEncoder</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=\operatorname*{PromptEncoder}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}=r_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}=r_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be router scores. To discourage collapse onto a few experts, we maximize the entropy of distribution <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\tau}=\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{s}/\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\tau}=\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{s}/\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>, implemented as a loss:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}\;=\;-\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\!\left[\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(\pi_{\tau}\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.684em;" width="0.684em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}\;=\;-\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\!\left[\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(\pi_{\tau}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We use a straight-through (ST) relaxation: <em id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hard</em> Top-<math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> indices are used in the forward pass; gradients flow through the <em id="A2.p3.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">soft</em> <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> in the backward pass. A standard choice is Gumbel-perturbed scores <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{s}+\mathbf{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{s}+\mathbf{g}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.i.d. <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}</annotation></semantics></math> Gumbel) with temperature <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, yielding stable SoftTopK relaxations while preserving discrete routing at inference.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Load balancing.</span>
Within a batch of size <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{m}=\tfrac{1}{B}\sum_{i=0}^{B-1}\mathbf{1}[\,m\in\mathcal{I}^{(i)}_{\mathrm{active}}\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>active</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m}=\tfrac{1}{B}\sum_{i=0}^{B-1}\mathbf{1}[\,m\in\mathcal{I}^{(i)}_{\mathrm{active}}\,]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the activation frequency of expert <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. We penalize the squared coefficient of variation to encourage uniform utilization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}\;=\;\Big(\tfrac{\mathrm{std}(\mathbf{f})}{\mathrm{mean}(\mathbf{f})}\Big)^{2},\qquad\mathbf{f}=(f_{0},\ldots,f_{M-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>std</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>mean</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}\;=\;\Big(\tfrac{\mathrm{std}(\mathbf{f})}{\mathrm{mean}(\mathbf{f})}\Big)^{2},\qquad\mathbf{f}=(f_{0},\ldots,f_{M-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Routing-consistency (stability under small routing changes).</span>
Discrete Top-<math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> selections can vary due to stochastic perturbations; we regularize for stability by sampling two <em id="A2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independent</em> relaxed selections for the same input. Concretely, draw <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{0},\mathbf{g}_{1}\sim\mathrm{Gumbel}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>Gumbel</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{0},\mathbf{g}_{1}\sim\mathrm{Gumbel}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and form <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{j}=(\mathbf{s}+\mathbf{g}_{j})/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{j}=(\mathbf{s}+\mathbf{g}_{j})/\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <em id="A2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hard</em> Top-<math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for the forward pass (primary distribution <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(0)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(0)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), and in parallel we compute a distribution <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> using experts selected via <math id="A2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We minimize token-wise KL divergence between the two distributions over the target tokens:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{con}}\;=\;\frac{1}{2T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big(\mathrm{KL}\!\big(p^{(0)}_{t}\,\|\,p^{(1)}_{t}\big)\;+\;\mathrm{KL}\!\big(p^{(1)}_{t}\,\|\,p^{(0)}_{t}\big)\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>con</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{con}}\;=\;\frac{1}{2T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big(\mathrm{KL}\!\big(p^{(0)}_{t}\,\|\,p^{(1)}_{t}\big)\;+\;\mathrm{KL}\!\big(p^{(1)}_{t}\,\|\,p^{(0)}_{t}\big)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total objective.</span>
The full loss combines the above terms:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{total}}\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{LM}}\;+\;\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}\;+\;\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}}\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}\;+\;\lambda_{\mathrm{con}}\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{con}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>total</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>LM</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>con</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>con</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{total}}\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{LM}}\;+\;\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}\;+\;\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}}\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}\;+\;\lambda_{\mathrm{con}}\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{con}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">We use AdamW with weight decay, gradient clipping, and warmup. Weights <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}},\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}},\lambda_{\mathrm{con}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>con</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}},\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}},\lambda_{\mathrm{con}})</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed; the defaults used in our experiments are <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{con}}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>con</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{con}}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> MoT Training (single batch step)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inputs:</span> batch <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, router <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, projectors <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{\text{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{\text{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math>, cross-attn <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math>, frozen experts <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}_{m}\}_{m=0}^{M-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}_{m}\}_{m=0}^{M-1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           Encode prompt: <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\operatorname*{PromptEncoder}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">PromptEncoder</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\operatorname*{PromptEncoder}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>;  <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}\leftarrow r_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\leftarrow r_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
           Sample <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{0}\!\sim\!\mathrm{Gumbel}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∼</mo><msup><mi>Gumbel</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{0}\!\sim\!\mathrm{Gumbel}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, form <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{0}=(\mathbf{s}+\mathbf{g}_{0})/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{0}=(\mathbf{s}+\mathbf{g}_{0})/\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, select <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}=\text{TopK}(\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>TopK</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}=\text{TopK}(\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
           Run active experts with interaction layers; primary <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> produces distributions <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p^{(0)}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p^{(0)}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math>; compute <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{LM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>LM</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{LM}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
           Compute router entropy loss <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}=-\mathcal{H}(\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{s}/\tau))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}=-\mathcal{H}(\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{s}/\tau))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
           Compute load balance loss <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}=\big(\mathrm{std}(\mathbf{f})/\mathrm{mean}(\mathbf{f})\big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>std</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>mean</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}=\big(\mathrm{std}(\mathbf{f})/\mathrm{mean}(\mathbf{f})\big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}=(f_{0},\ldots,f_{M-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}=(f_{0},\ldots,f_{M-1})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
           Sample <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{1}\!\sim\!\mathrm{Gumbel}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∼</mo><msup><mi>Gumbel</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{1}\!\sim\!\mathrm{Gumbel}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, form <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{1}=(\mathbf{s}+\mathbf{g}_{1})/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{1}=(\mathbf{s}+\mathbf{g}_{1})/\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, select <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{\prime}_{\text{act}}=\text{TopK}(\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>TopK</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{\prime}_{\text{act}}=\text{TopK}(\tilde{\mathbf{s}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
           Run secondary active experts <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{\prime}_{\text{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{\prime}_{\text{act}}</annotation></semantics></math> with interaction layers; obtain <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p^{(1)}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p^{(1)}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math>; compute <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{con}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>con</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{con}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
           Combine: <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{total}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{LM}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{con}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{con}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>total</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>LM</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>con</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>con</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{total}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{LM}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ent}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{bal}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{bal}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{con}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{con}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
           Update trainable parameters <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{\theta},\Theta_{\text{proj}},\Theta_{\text{attn}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{\theta},\Theta_{\text{proj}},\Theta_{\text{attn}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (experts frozen) using AdamW

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Inference</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MoT inference proceeds in two phases: <em id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">prefill</em> and <em id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">decode</em>. The router selects a sparse set of experts; all selected experts advance their own token streams to maintain latent trajectories, while the <em id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">primary</em> expert produces the final output sequence. Standard causal masking is used in the cross-attention computed within the interaction layers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prefill.</span>
Given input <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, compute <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=\operatorname*{PromptEncoder}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">PromptEncoder</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=\operatorname*{PromptEncoder}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, scores <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}=r_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}=r_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})</annotation></semantics></math>, select <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}=\text{TopK}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>TopK</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}=\text{TopK}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math>, and choose the primary <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}=\arg\max_{m\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}}s_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}=\arg\max_{m\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}}s_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Run a forward pass of all active experts on <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> with interaction layers enabled. Cache standard backbone KV pairs and the interaction-layer KV projections at every stack for each active expert. Each active expert emits its next token; the primary token is appended to the output sequence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decode.</span>
At step <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\!\geq\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\!\geq\!0</annotation></semantics></math>, each active expert <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> receives its own previous token (the primary expert receives the last output token). Using KV caches, the tokens traverse through the stacks. At each interaction layer, every active expert updates its KV cache; the primary expert’s query token attends over the concatenated KV from all active experts to update its hidden state. New tokens are produced for all active experts; only the primary token is appended to the output. Decoding continues until the primary emits <span id="A3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;EOS&gt;</span> or the maximum sequence length is reached. If a non-primary expert emits <span id="A3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;EOS&gt;</span> earlier, its subsequent tokens are treated as padding and are masked in the interaction layers.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.21164v1/masked_attn.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/230;" width="548" height="230"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Attention mask used for the cross-attention computation in the interaction layers. The cross-attention is computed between queries from the primary expert and keys/values from the active experts (including the primary expert). The generated token from each active expert after prefill (shown in green) add to the KV cache for the interaction layer.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> MoT Inference (single sequence)</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> prompt <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, experts <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}_{m}\}_{m=0}^{M-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}_{m}\}_{m=0}^{M-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (frozen), router <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, projectors <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{\text{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{\text{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math>, cross-attn <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math>, max length <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Route:</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\!\leftarrow\!\operatorname*{PromptEncoder}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.0539em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.0539em" rspace="0em">PromptEncoder</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\!\leftarrow\!\operatorname*{PromptEncoder}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>;  <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}\!\leftarrow\!r_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\!\leftarrow\!r_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})</annotation></semantics></math>;  <math id="alg2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}\!\leftarrow\!\text{TopK}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>TopK</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}\!\leftarrow\!\text{TopK}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math>;  <math id="alg2.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}\!\leftarrow\!\arg\max_{m\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}}s_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}\!\leftarrow\!\arg\max_{m\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}}s_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prefill:</span> run all <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\!\in\!\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\!\in\!\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> with interaction layers; cache backbone KV and interaction-layer KV at each stack; obtain next-token logits for each active expert; append the primary token to output <math id="alg2.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
           Initialize step <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\!\leftarrow\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\!\leftarrow\!0</annotation></semantics></math>;  mark all <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\!\in\!\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\!\in\!\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">alive</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">alive</span>  and <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{y}|&lt;T_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{y}|&lt;T_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{act}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">alive</span> <span id="alg2.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
              feed previous token of expert <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> through its stacks using KV caches

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
              at each interaction layer: update KV cache for expert <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, also form the query token using the current primary token and attend over concatenated KV from all active experts (padding masked)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
              produce next token for expert <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="alg2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> this is the output token)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
              <span id="alg2.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> token is <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;EOS&gt;</span> and <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
               mark <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> as <span id="alg2.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dead</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
              <span id="alg2.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg2.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
              treat token as padding for <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> (no compute; masked in interaction)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg2.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
            append the primary token to <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>;  if <span id="alg2.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;EOS&gt;</span> for <math id="alg2.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> then stop

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return</span> <math id="alg2.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
