<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Additional Experiments</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Motivation.</span> A potential concern with multi-benchmark evaluations (Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Mixture of Thoughts: Learning to Aggregate What Experts Think, Not Just What They Say" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) is overlap between training and evaluation data. Such leakage could artificially inflate performance on both ID and OOD tasks. To address this, we conduct additional experiments following the same setup as before, but with separation between training and evaluation datasets. This ensures that our results fairly demonstrate the advantages of MoT over prior approaches.</p>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training datasets.</h4>

<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For training we use the following datasets: commonsense and multi-choice QA (35% of steps; HellaSwag, CommonsenseQA, ARC-Challenge), math and quantitative reasoning (25%; GSM8K, SVAMP), code generation (25%; MBPP and a 10k subset of APPS), and reading comprehension (15%; SQuAD v2).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sampling and batching.</h4>

<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Percentages above denote the share of <em id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">optimizer updates</em> allocated to each domain: at each update we sample a domain with probabilities <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0.35,0.25,0.25,0.15)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.35</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.15</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0.35,0.25,0.25,0.15)</annotation></semantics></math> and then draw the batch from a dataset within that domain using temperature-based sampling (temperature <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=2.0</annotation></semantics></math>). We use a sequence length of <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2048</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2048</annotation></semantics></math> and a batch size of 64.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h4>

<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train and evaluate using the same seven 7B to 8B experts. Training setting is identical to that in Sec. <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Additional Experiments ‣ Mixture of Thoughts: Learning to Aggregate What Experts Think, Not Just What They Say" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>. We report accuracy for benchmarks that are <em id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> used for training.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A9.T15" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 15: </span><span id="A9.T15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Additional experiments (standard training configuration).</span> Accuracy (%, higher is better) on evaluation benchmarks not used for MoT training.
For baselines, “ID” refers to datasets included in their training; “OOD” refers to held-out datasets.
For MoT, <em id="A9.T15.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> evaluation datasets are OOD since none were used for training.</figcaption>
<div id="A9.T15.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:62.4pt;vertical-align:-29.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-113.6pt,17.8pt) scale(0.63621631286643,0.63621631286643) ;">
